WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.725
Now what the program teaches.

2
00:00:01.725 --> 00:00:03.988
It separates education from training.

3
00:00:03.988 --> 00:00:08.559
Education builds the mental model,
for everyone, before any tool,

4
00:00:08.559 --> 00:00:13.649
and it teaches six ideas in order,
because each depends on the one before.

5
00:00:13.649 --> 00:00:16.650
Governance is a system
that runs continuously.

6
00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:18.712
Identity is the starting point.

7
00:00:18.712 --> 00:00:21.549
One map replaces many inventories.

8
00:00:21.549 --> 00:00:24.762
Every derived record names
its source and version.

9
00:00:24.762 --> 00:00:29.874
Modernization is a lifecycle under
change control, not a project that ends.

10
00:00:29.874 --> 00:00:32.038
And drift is the feedback signal.

11
00:00:32.038 --> 00:00:36.510
Someone who holds those ideas understands
why the help desk now asks for

12
00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:39.789
verification, why a role is
activated instead of held,

13
00:00:39.789 --> 00:00:41.950
and why a screenshot isn't evidence.

14
00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:46.591
Orientation comes as a ninety-minute
walkthrough, a self-serve written path,

15
00:00:46.591 --> 00:00:50.275
and a forty-five-minute briefing
for auditors and assessors.

16
00:00:50.275 --> 00:00:54.035
Training comes after, by role,
in four tracks: compliance,

17
00:00:54.035 --> 00:00:58.858
for people who evidence controls;
implementation, for people who build;

18
00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:03.820
vendor training and labs; and end-user
training for everyone who signs in.
